e quota == nil` arm placed BETWEEN the last existing repo arm and the audit arm (the convention is store → parent repos → own repo → authz? → quota → jobs? → audit), and the Create unit of work grows a `svc.quota.Reserve(ctx, tx, key.OrganizationID, string(QuotaResource<Name>))` call placed AFTER every existence/parent-lookup check and BEFORE the desired-state Insert so a 404 on the parent is never disguised as a quota rejection AND a row-level conflict (slug, prefix, unique constraint) rolls the reservation back with the rest of the unit of work. (3) Constructor call-site fanout — three call sites change: cmd/yalla-api/main.go grows a `<name>Quota := noopQuotaReserver{}` placeholder (the real quota.Checker adapter is wired separately by a cross-cutting plan-resolver story; placeholder mirrors the projectQuota / environmentQuota / serviceQuota convention exactly), the in-package `package store` constructor-nil test grows a `nopQuotaReserver{}` local + a new `{nil quota, ...}` case wedged BETWEEN the last existing nil case and the audit case (positional ordering must mirror the constructor's nil-guard switch), and the `package store_test` integration-test helper grows the shared `&recordingQuota{}` (defined in projectservice_test.go — not a local `noopQuotaReserver{}`, which is only visible to cmd/yalla-api; the store_test package has its OWN allow-all fake hierarchy and the convention is to reuse `recordingQuota` for happy-path constructors). (4) Concurrent integration test — clone of the BE-0336 concurrent_deployments test with five structural simplifications when the owning service has no Authorizer / JobEnqueuer ports (api_keys is pure Yalla identity with no Dokploy mirror, so APIKeyService takes neither): no `atomicAuthorizer` / `atomicJobs` fakes need to be defined or counted; no `authz.calls == attempts` and no `jobs.calls == successes` assertions; the per-goroutine input loop calls `auth.Generate()` INSIDE the goroutine so every concurrent attempt mints its o